⍝ Quad_JSON

      ⍝ error cases...
⍝@ test3.


      ⍝ extra token
      ⎕JSON ' 33 44 '
LENGTH ERROR+
      ⎕JSON ' 33 44 '
      ^
      )MORE
⎕JSON B: there were extra tokens in B (tokenized: 2, but processed: 1).
    The JSON string must be one serialized value.

      ⍝ missing array separator
      ⍝/
      ⎕JSON '[42 52]'
DOMAIN ERROR+
      ⎕JSON '[42 52]'
      ^
      )MORE
⎕JSON B: Got '5' when expecting ',' at 4↓B

      )SIC

      ⍝ invalid escape sequences (Blake McBride, Bugs21 #4a) --------
      ⍝ RFC 8259 permits exactly \" \\ \/ \b \f \n \r \t (and \uXXXX,
      ⍝ tested separately above); any other 1-character escape used
      ⍝ to be silently accepted and decoded as the literal character
      ⍝ itself. Now rejected.

      ⎕JSON '["a\xb"]'
DOMAIN ERROR+
      ⎕JSON '["a\xb"]'
      ^
      )MORE
⎕JSON B: invalid escape sequence \x at 3↓B

      )SIC

      ⎕JSON '["a\qb"]'
DOMAIN ERROR+
      ⎕JSON '["a\qb"]'
      ^
      )MORE
⎕JSON B: invalid escape sequence \q at 3↓B

      )SIC

      ⍝ the already-valid 1-character escapes still all work
      ⍝
      ⎕JSON ' "a\\b"'
a\b

      ⎕JSON ' "a\/b"'
a/b

      ⎕UCS ⎕JSON ' "a\bb"'
97 8 98

      ⎕UCS ⎕JSON ' "a\fb"'
97 12 98

      ⎕UCS ⎕JSON ' "a\nb"'
97 10 98

      ⎕UCS ⎕JSON ' "a\rb"'
97 13 98

      ⎕UCS ⎕JSON ' "a\tb"'
97 9 98

      ⍝ leading zeros in numbers (Blake McBride, Bugs21 #4b) --------
      ⍝ RFC 8259: int = zero / (digit1-9 *DIGIT) -- a leading zero
      ⍝ used to be silently accepted with the extra digits kept.

      ⎕JSON '[0123]'
DOMAIN ERROR+
      ⎕JSON '[0123]'
      ^
      )MORE
⎕JSON B: malformed number (leading zero) at 1↓B

      )SIC

      ⎕JSON '[01]'
DOMAIN ERROR+
      ⎕JSON '[01]'
      ^
      )MORE
⎕JSON B: malformed number (leading zero) at 1↓B

      )SIC

      ⎕JSON '[-01]'
DOMAIN ERROR+
      ⎕JSON '[-01]'
      ^
      )MORE
⎕JSON B: malformed number (leading zero) at 1↓B

      )SIC

      ⍝ a lone "0" (not followed by further digits) is still fine
      ⍝
      ⎕JSON '[0]'
0

      ⎕JSON '[0.5]'
0.5

      ⎕JSON '[00]'
DOMAIN ERROR+
      ⎕JSON '[00]'
      ^
      )MORE
⎕JSON B: malformed number (leading zero) at 1↓B

      )SIC

      ⍝ number
      ⎕JSON '33'
33

      ⎕JSON '33.3 '
33.3

      ⍝ string
      ⎕JSON ' "hello"'
hello

      ⎕JSON ' "he\"lo"'
he"lo

      ⎕UCS ⎕JSON ' "he\u0007lo"'
104 101 7 108 111

      ⍝ example from JSON RFC 8259
      ⎕JSON '"\uD834\uDD1E"'
𝄞

      ⎕JSON '"a\uD834\uDD1Eb"'
a𝄞b

      ⍝ JSON array
      ⎕JSON '[1, 2, .3, 3E4, 5.6E¯7, -1 ]'
1 2 0.3 30000 5.6E¯7 ¯1


      ⍝ JSON object
      ⎕JSON 36 ⎕CR """
      { "a": 1,
      "b": 2,
      "c": "ccc",
      "dd" : 3,
      "Ee" : 3E4,
      "f" : 5.6E¯7,
      "G:" :  -1
      }
      """
.Ee: 30000

.G:: ¯1

.a:  1

.b:  2

.c:  ┌→──┐
     │ccc│
     └───┘

.dd: 3

.f:  5.6E¯7

      ⍝ JSON literals
      ⍝
      8 ⎕CR ⎕JSON '[42, "s", "string", null, true, false ]'
┌→──────────────────────────────────────────┐
│42 ┌→┐ ┌→─────┐ ┌──────┐ ┌──────┐ ┌───────┐│
│   │s│ │string│ │┌→───┐│ │┌→───┐│ │┌→────┐││
│   └─┘ └──────┘ ││null││ ││true││ ││false│││
│                │└────┘│ │└────┘│ │└─────┘││
│                └ϵ─────┘ └ϵ─────┘ └ϵ──────┘│
└ϵϵ─────────────────────────────────────────┘

